This file should should discover what platform is accommodating the program and ammend the ini file accordingly.
This file should call lang_sel.py if the ini doesn't state the users language.
This file should call modules/name_call_sel.py if ini doesn't contain a name in the call= entry.
This file should call find_rad.py if the ini doesn't  contain port, baud, model.
This file then should interact with chat_int.py communicating with the radio and passing cleaned responses for chat_int.py to display to the user.
Cleaning means removing trailing and leading zweros and inserting a decimal point between megahertz and kilohertz.
Translating MD01 to LSB and other output to human readable format. The label mechanism for each language should be used which chat_int.py should display language defined labels.
New labels must be provided for every supported language.

Paths:

All labels must be sourced from the path according to the language selected by the user 
/yac/lang/en/labels
${HOME}/yac/lang/de/labels
${HOME}/yac/lang/pl/labels

Likewise for language specific help tags.
${HOME}/yac/lang/en/help
${HOME}/yac/lang/de/help
${HOME}/yac/lang/pl/help

All radio controll commands read and set must be in this path. Each new radio will use a model identifier inside which set and read subdirectories. The example is the Yaesu FT-DX10.
${HOME}/yac/rad_cmds/yaesu/CAT/models/0761/read/
${HOME}/yac/rad_cmds/yaesu/CAT/models/0761/set/
${HOME}/yac/rad_cmds/yaesu/CAT/common/read/
${HOME}/yac/rad_cmds/yaesu/CAT/common/set/

For tidiness small module units are found.
${HOME}/yac/modules

This file and yac.ini
${HOME}/yac/


